WEBVTT

00:01:37.370 --> 00:01:41.070
Does this look like a game to you?
Like an artificial world?

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:45.210
This is all real. Everything is.

00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:52.180
Shizuno-sempai, wait!

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:01.220
It was real?

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:05.390
But, then... Why did my hand disappear?

00:02:16.310 --> 00:02:17.240
Hayase.

00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:21.650
Wha... Hey!

00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:23.620
Hey, wait a sec!

00:02:26.190 --> 00:02:27.820
Hayase, are you...

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:29.150
No, I'm not.

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:32.330
If I apologized,
would you come back then?

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:35.320
An apology means nothing
when it's not sincere.

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:38.270
No way, really?!
It's just common sense these days!

00:02:38.270 --> 00:02:40.370
You think so?
Aren't you embarrassed, though?

00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:41.700
Not a bit!

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:43.670
I'm sorry!

00:02:45.110 --> 00:02:46.840
That's Kyo over there.

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:48.670
And Hayasechi...

00:02:49.910 --> 00:02:51.470
Huh? Hayasechi?

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:53.670
I'm totally sincere right now.

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:56.340
I wasn't thinking about
the consequences before.

00:02:57.350 --> 00:02:58.990
I made the foul,

00:02:58.990 --> 00:03:01.510
and I was wrong to punch that
referee during the preliminaries.

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:04.030
They wiped out all your scores too,
because of me.

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:06.030
This isn't like you.

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:10.260
I've had stuff happen to me lately.
And I've had time to think things over.

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:12.600
I'm still confused about stuff,

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:15.540
but my real feelings about things
have started to come through.

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:16.800
So, let's patch things up...

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:19.600
We don't do what you want
for your convenience!

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:25.270
We three made a decision that day.
We'll never swim with you again!

00:03:26.150 --> 00:03:29.120
That's why I quit swimming...

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:36.590
Huh? I've seen this before...

00:03:37.460 --> 00:03:40.260
He says nothing,
and just watches him walk away...

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:42.160
Maybe it's déjà vu.

00:03:49.070 --> 00:03:51.700
Wait! I just got that feeling, too.

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:56.910
<i>...and the results of a reexamination of Shanghai</i>
<i>show a very low probability of any survivors.</i>

00:03:56.910 --> 00:03:59.640
<i>Rescue operations have been suspended.</i>

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:08.310
<i>This is reality!</i>

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:17.570
Morning, Sogoru!

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:17.830
Yo!

00:04:19.270 --> 00:04:20.730
<i>This is reality!</i>

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:23.400
Well, my folks sent it to me, actually.

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:25.370
Oh! Well, thank you so much!

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:28.710
Higuma manjuu buns,
a Hokkaido specialty.

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:31.520
- They always send me, like, two dozen of these things.
- Oh, wow! He's aiming high, isn't he?

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:32.710
- Oh, wow! He's aiming high, isn't he?
- You don't say!

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:34.700
Some people play outside their league.

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:37.410
Hey! I heard that!

00:04:37.550 --> 00:04:40.490
<i>Here is my school.</i>
<i>Here are my teachers.</i>

00:04:40.890 --> 00:04:43.120
<i>Along with everyone else.</i>

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:49.560
Why don't you buy a console already?!

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:50.890
What's the problem?!

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:57.000
<i>Yesterday leads to today.</i>

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:59.210
<i>Today will lead to tomorrow.</i>

00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:01.230
<i>That's reality!</i>

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:09.840
<i>This is reality?!</i>

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:17.730
Sword!

00:05:17.730 --> 00:05:18.090
Roger!

00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:28.340
Mission, accomplished.

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:29.300
Returning to ship.

00:05:31.970 --> 00:05:33.740
Thank you! You saved me!

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:36.880
Is she <i>still</i> mad at me?

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:39.310
<i>Transmission range, reached.</i>

00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:42.120
Transmitting. Entangle, time out.

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:44.080
<i>Entangle, time out.</i>

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:03.330
So, which is the "real" world?

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:07.630
The story of the butterfly dream.
You know it?

00:06:08.980 --> 00:06:11.110
The truth is,
everyone goes through this.

00:06:11.110 --> 00:06:14.120
You wonder if the "you"
you are now is the real "you."

00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:16.140
Especially people at your age.

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:19.250
Like you wonder if
you're really the child...

00:06:19.250 --> 00:06:21.240
of a rich family
somewhere or something.

00:06:21.420 --> 00:06:24.060
No. It's not really like that.

00:06:24.060 --> 00:06:28.330
Everybody wants to believe that
there's something special about them.

00:06:28.330 --> 00:06:31.470
When we're young and our world is
essentially limited to our families,

00:06:31.470 --> 00:06:34.160
we always feel like we're special.

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:38.270
But as we grow up, we come
to realize that we're ordinary.

00:06:38.270 --> 00:06:43.010
And we start to resent thinking of
ourselves as average and run-of-the-mill.

00:06:43.410 --> 00:06:47.150
Those who don't want to face
this escape into fantasy worlds,

00:06:47.150 --> 00:06:49.840
and become convinced that their
fantasy world is the real one.

00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:54.220
That they pilot robots in another
world, fighting an evil enemy.

00:06:54.860 --> 00:06:56.860
That you're special, somehow.

00:06:56.860 --> 00:06:58.920
That you're a "cerebrant" or whatever.

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:01.560
Sensei, what are?

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:05.130
When Chuang Tzu dreamed he was a
butterfly, he wondered upon awakening...

00:07:05.130 --> 00:07:08.120
whether he was actually a
butterfly dreaming he was a man.

00:07:09.100 --> 00:07:12.140
Personally, it doesn't matter
to me which is which.

00:07:12.140 --> 00:07:14.200
I choose as I please.

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:16.430
As you... please?

00:07:16.610 --> 00:07:17.450
However...

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:19.310
If one world is reality,

00:07:19.310 --> 00:07:22.040
then it follows that the
other must be fiction.

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:24.510
Maybe both worlds are an illusion.

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:31.380
Or whatever. You start thinking
about stuff like that at our age.

00:07:31.790 --> 00:07:34.890
Like, am I really alive or not?
Stuff like that.

00:07:35.430 --> 00:07:38.990
That's why I always have so
much fun talking to you, Sogoru!

00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:42.770
Hey! Tomigai, wait!

00:07:52.350 --> 00:07:53.750
Oh, they're pissing me off!

00:07:53.750 --> 00:07:55.750
You're consuming our Q.L. too rapidly!

00:07:55.750 --> 00:07:57.150
Don't waste your shots, please!

00:08:02.320 --> 00:08:03.720
If I'm out of ammo...

00:08:07.660 --> 00:08:10.430
there's always <i>this</i> way to fight!

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:26.170
I'm home.

00:08:29.980 --> 00:08:32.010
Late again, huh?

00:08:35.390 --> 00:08:38.290
Like always! How long...

00:08:44.700 --> 00:08:47.570
How long have I lived alone?

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:58.680
And that concludes this special
session of the student council.

00:09:01.250 --> 00:09:04.910
Huh? What?
Is it over? Miss Minato?

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:14.620
All right, now for the remaining topics.

00:09:14.730 --> 00:09:17.630
First of all, a status report on
Kyo Sogoru's recovery.

00:09:18.630 --> 00:09:20.940
This is the mentalism
data from Kyo Sogoru...

00:09:20.940 --> 00:09:23.060
gathered here over
the last few weeks.

00:09:23.340 --> 00:09:25.670
When compared
with the old version,

00:09:25.670 --> 00:09:30.340
all parameters have increased
between 50 and 85 percent.

00:09:30.740 --> 00:09:33.080
And the recovery of his mind
is proceeding well, too?

00:09:33.080 --> 00:09:36.980
Still, it's dangerous to let him return
to normal, in his case, at least.

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:39.820
Commander, we've detected the enemy.

00:09:40.290 --> 00:09:42.380
On our way.

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:45.220
Excuse me, but I forgot my...

00:09:46.660 --> 00:09:47.820
Huh?

00:09:54.870 --> 00:09:57.100
Ulvorfuls. They went to
stealth mode immediately,

00:09:57.100 --> 00:09:59.130
so they were only exposed
for a moment, but...

00:09:59.740 --> 00:10:01.980
They haven't spotted us, right?

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:05.780
The Oceanus's anti-radar and infra-red
Pellucidar mode is functioning perfectly.

00:10:05.950 --> 00:10:09.470
The chances of them spotting us
at this range are extremely low.

00:10:10.050 --> 00:10:12.490
They appear to be en route
back to their carrier.

00:10:12.490 --> 00:10:14.790
Analysis results of their
course movements...

00:10:14.790 --> 00:10:16.860
indicates their main
force may be close by.

00:10:16.860 --> 00:10:18.090
To Japan?!

00:10:18.090 --> 00:10:20.490
They've already knocked
out the Tokyo server.

00:10:20.490 --> 00:10:23.030
Could they be after the
Maihama server this time?

00:10:23.030 --> 00:10:25.090
Any of our allied ships in the area?

00:10:25.170 --> 00:10:27.360
The Dvaraka is in
the vicinity of Siberia.

00:10:27.470 --> 00:10:29.770
Request aid,
circumstances permitting.

00:10:32.370 --> 00:10:35.080
In short, when thinking in
terms of quantum mechanics,

00:10:35.080 --> 00:10:38.150
the interaction of elementary particle
spin can be a potential descriptor...

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:41.580
of the state matter assumes
from moment to moment.

00:10:41.580 --> 00:10:45.540
For example, assuming
a closed system for now,

00:10:45.650 --> 00:10:49.450
with the density value as the potential
descriptor, for everything in the system,

00:10:49.820 --> 00:10:53.380
the quantum state may be said
to be the potential operator.

00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:55.060
<i>How long has it been?</i>

00:10:56.100 --> 00:11:00.430
I have to get going.
Wake up already, Kyo!

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:06.330
<i>And why have I never thought to question it?</i>

00:11:06.570 --> 00:11:12.270
Now, let's describe the matter
composing an individual person as data.

00:11:12.650 --> 00:11:16.720
The cells, molecules, and atoms
which compose the physical body.

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:18.910
We now find ourselves presented with a problem.

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:21.120
In short, it's our consciousness.

00:11:21.120 --> 00:11:22.920
<i>It's like I'm remembering something...</i>

00:11:23.020 --> 00:11:25.630
You see, in quantum mechanics,

00:11:25.630 --> 00:11:30.290
while an observer can tell us when,
say, a wave form convergence occurs,

00:11:30.860 --> 00:11:34.960
nobody can observe an individual's
consciousness aside from the individual themself.

00:11:35.140 --> 00:11:37.000
Therefore, from the outside,

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:41.040
we can only know the quantum
state of someone's consciousness,

00:11:41.040 --> 00:11:45.270
but it's impossible for the outside
observer to extract that as data.

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:50.380
However, here we run into another bizarre
characteristic of quantum mechanics.

00:11:50.550 --> 00:11:54.760
In other words, if we make use of the
interaction effect between particles,

00:11:54.760 --> 00:12:00.460
it's possible to move that quantum
state entirely to another location.

00:12:00.460 --> 00:12:01.460
Welcome!

00:12:01.460 --> 00:12:05.170
However, in this case, we're
actually moving it, not copying it.

00:12:05.170 --> 00:12:08.100
In short, the original data disappears.

00:12:08.100 --> 00:12:10.830
<i>If one is reality, the other is fiction...</i>

00:12:11.410 --> 00:12:15.140
This particle interaction which
allows for quantum teleportation...

00:12:15.140 --> 00:12:16.840
is known as an "entanglement."

00:12:18.980 --> 00:12:19.910
Entanglement?!

00:12:20.310 --> 00:12:22.840
<i>They've already knocked</i>
<i>out the Tokyo server.</i>

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:26.920
Hm? What's wrong, Sogoru?

00:12:28.460 --> 00:12:29.590
Sogoru, what is it?!

00:12:29.590 --> 00:12:32.020
Sogoru! Sogoru!

00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:40.530
What's wrong with me?!

00:12:41.300 --> 00:12:41.860
Kyo!

00:12:42.670 --> 00:12:44.330
You heard it, didn't you?

00:12:45.310 --> 00:12:46.530
It's a mission.

00:12:51.780 --> 00:12:53.300
Kyo?

00:12:53.880 --> 00:12:56.550
<i>Yehl, what happened to Kyo?</i>

00:12:56.550 --> 00:12:58.420
He's going to be late.

00:12:58.420 --> 00:13:00.420
<i>What's keeping him?!</i>

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:02.850
<i>Lu-shen and May-yen are</i>
<i>already hunting for the enemy!</i>

00:13:03.390 --> 00:13:05.550
<i>As soon as Kyo arrives, move out!</i>

00:13:06.330 --> 00:13:07.550
Understood.

00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:17.330
Huh?

00:13:22.980 --> 00:13:25.210
I don't see the enemy anywhere.

00:13:26.750 --> 00:13:28.950
This is Zegapain Garuda.

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:31.650
<i>Returning to ship for Q.L. replenishment.</i>

00:13:31.650 --> 00:13:34.250
Perhaps we miscalculated their course.

00:13:44.100 --> 00:13:47.870
23 degrees, bearing to starboard!
Enemies sighted! Range: 1500!

00:13:47.870 --> 00:13:48.990
What did you say?!

00:13:49.500 --> 00:13:51.770
Two units... Three... No!

00:13:51.770 --> 00:13:54.370
Twenty-eight, twenty-nine, still increasing!

00:13:58.350 --> 00:13:59.550
They were waiting for us!

00:13:59.550 --> 00:14:03.920
Those Ulvorfuls we first spotted were
just bait to draw us here into their trap!

00:14:04.620 --> 00:14:07.640
Contact Kyo now!
Emergency launch the Altair!

00:14:08.020 --> 00:14:11.320
Kyo Sogoru is off-line!
I can't make contact with him!

00:14:16.160 --> 00:14:19.600
Well, it can't be helped.
I can't go there now.

00:14:19.970 --> 00:14:23.460
Oh well, guess they'll just have
to manage without me.

00:14:23.640 --> 00:14:27.160
Ship, shift to defensive mode!
Releasing locks on all weaponry!

00:14:27.310 --> 00:14:30.810
Raising defense field
around ship... Complete!

00:14:30.810 --> 00:14:33.150
Activating point defense systems!

00:14:33.150 --> 00:14:34.410
He's hesitating?

00:14:34.410 --> 00:14:37.320
Yes, between existing here and in Maihama.

00:14:37.320 --> 00:14:40.790
You could call it a failure of his brain to adapt...

00:14:40.790 --> 00:14:43.290
to how quickly he comes and
goes between the two worlds.

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:45.190
When will he return to normal?

00:14:45.190 --> 00:14:48.950
I don't know. It's possible he may never return.

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:50.360
That can't be!

00:15:07.480 --> 00:15:10.680
Look, I know I've never said
it before, but the truth is l...

00:15:10.680 --> 00:15:12.520
Wait! We're not ready for this!

00:15:12.620 --> 00:15:15.060
But the fact is that I love you!

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:17.460
Even if the world were to end,

00:15:17.460 --> 00:15:19.820
this love will last forever!

00:15:22.700 --> 00:15:25.530
What's wrong? Come on, next line!

00:15:26.270 --> 00:15:30.070
Isn't this a little overblown?
It's not realistic!

00:15:30.070 --> 00:15:31.510
You think so?

00:15:31.510 --> 00:15:35.240
Look, I rewrote this because
you threatened to quit last time!

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:37.570
Um, look, the reason for that was...

00:15:37.980 --> 00:15:39.840
Hey! What's this?!

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:44.410
Oh, wow! I can't believe that's
still here! That takes me back!

00:15:45.150 --> 00:15:46.520
You wrote that?

00:15:46.520 --> 00:15:49.360
It was back in kindergarten, remember?

00:15:49.360 --> 00:15:52.760
When you stole my doll
and threw it away that time.

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:56.660
Oh... Yeah, I remember!
I'm sorry about that! No prob then...

00:15:57.100 --> 00:16:00.360
Wait, I went nuts looking for
that doll and brought it back!

00:16:03.200 --> 00:16:04.760
I guess you did. No prob.

00:16:09.680 --> 00:16:12.110
Especially since you came
to read my script with me.

00:16:13.850 --> 00:16:16.510
Hold it...
Haven't we done this before?

00:16:17.250 --> 00:16:19.890
Reading the script here
and finding that graffiti...

00:16:19.890 --> 00:16:21.650
Except...

00:16:21.920 --> 00:16:23.890
Something's different...

00:16:28.530 --> 00:16:32.930
The rain...
No. It wasn't raining the last time.

00:16:32.930 --> 00:16:34.960
What are you saying?

00:16:37.640 --> 00:16:40.570
What is it?
This awful feeling I have?

00:16:41.010 --> 00:16:43.140
Suspend Pellucidar mode operation!

00:16:43.140 --> 00:16:46.740
Divert all ships resources for support
of the Zegas and our defenses!

00:17:03.800 --> 00:17:06.160
<i>Something's wrong... Very, VERY wrong!</i>

00:17:06.730 --> 00:17:11.670
<i>Defense field generators 3 and 6,</i>
<i>output down 45 percent! Overload!</i>

00:17:11.670 --> 00:17:14.040
- <i>Bring on 12 and 13 as reserve!</i>
- <i>Sealing of damaged areas now complete!</i>

00:17:16.980 --> 00:17:18.310
<i>Reserve systems, activated!</i>

00:17:18.380 --> 00:17:19.500
Kyo...

00:17:21.920 --> 00:17:24.150
Kaminagi... I've gotta go.

00:17:25.990 --> 00:17:28.060
I made a promise to Shizuno-sempai.

00:17:28.060 --> 00:17:30.020
That I would save this world.

00:17:30.690 --> 00:17:31.880
Kyo, wait!

00:17:43.270 --> 00:17:45.970
Damn! No time to replenish my Q.L.!

00:17:46.210 --> 00:17:49.680
Please let me launch in Zegatank!
I can give him a Q.L. charge!

00:17:49.680 --> 00:17:51.680
The Caladrius would be useless out there!

00:17:51.680 --> 00:17:54.080
Unless we break out of this encirclement,
we can't transmit you!

00:17:54.380 --> 00:17:55.710
Any sign of our backup?!

00:17:55.850 --> 00:17:59.050
The Dvaraka says they're sending us a mercenary.

00:17:59.250 --> 00:18:00.690
Mercenary?

00:18:02.260 --> 00:18:03.090
Kyo Sogoru!

00:18:06.490 --> 00:18:08.930
Zegapain Altair, prepare for launch!

00:18:14.870 --> 00:18:16.770
<i>Combat Q.L., depleted.</i>

00:18:16.770 --> 00:18:18.430
Lu-shen, over there!

00:18:33.320 --> 00:18:35.720
Q.L. charge now at 43 percent!

00:18:36.120 --> 00:18:37.110
That'll do!

00:18:46.330 --> 00:18:48.600
Q.L. charge, successful.

00:18:48.600 --> 00:18:50.070
Sorry I was late!

00:18:50.070 --> 00:18:51.340
<i>This is beyond late!</i>

00:18:51.340 --> 00:18:52.400
Then let's do this!

00:19:15.360 --> 00:19:18.430
They're concentrating their fire
on Garuda and Altair!

00:19:18.430 --> 00:19:19.960
Don't let them escape
with any combat data!

00:19:21.000 --> 00:19:23.160
Wipe out all enemies in this area!

00:19:38.990 --> 00:19:40.820
It's over.

00:19:40.820 --> 00:19:42.950
That wasn't so bad, was it?

00:19:48.130 --> 00:19:49.620
Isn't that?

00:20:04.040 --> 00:20:05.480
This is!

00:20:14.520 --> 00:20:15.990
Maihama?

00:20:18.830 --> 00:20:21.950
Yes. This is Maihama.

00:20:22.500 --> 00:20:24.520
The <i>real</i> Maihama.

00:20:27.730 --> 00:20:28.670
<i>Warning!</i>

00:20:45.490 --> 00:20:47.350
Dammit!

00:21:04.040 --> 00:21:05.130
Hu... man?!

00:21:09.210 --> 00:21:11.070
What the hell is this?

00:21:12.650 --> 00:21:14.010
Abyss.

00:22:51.410 --> 00:22:53.250
Abyss and Sin.

00:22:53.250 --> 00:22:56.950
The demon soldiers of the Gards-orm
who have killed many, many Cerebrants.

00:22:56.950 --> 00:22:59.420
Retreat at once, Kyo!
You mustn't fight them!

00:22:59.950 --> 00:23:03.320
You have to recover the memories
you lost as soon as you can!

00:23:03.920 --> 00:23:06.790
About what is reality
and what is made-up.

00:23:07.390 --> 00:23:10.460
About what exists
and what are just phantoms.

00:23:10.460 --> 00:23:13.230
The time has come to face
the reality of the world!

00:23:14.000 --> 00:23:16.900
Next time, on Zegapain: "Meta-Body."

00:23:16.900 --> 00:23:20.030
My thoughts, never to be erased.
